    },
    {
      "id": "1e766f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "Thank you for your interest in Sacramento State! This articulation agreement displays the lower-division courses required in the major: Sacramento State courses on the left and approved (articulated) transfer courses on the right. Students are advised to complete the lower-division coursework in this agreement prior to transfer. Additional Resources: See the University Catalog for the full listing of degree requirements for this major. Visit our Sac State Apply page for more information about our campus! Visit the Admissions website for current transfer admission requirements. Connect with an Admissions Counselor .",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Thank you for your interest in Sacramento State! </strong></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">This articulation agreement displays the lower-division courses required in the major: Sacramento State courses on the left and approved (articulated) transfer courses on the right. Students are advised to complete the lower-division coursework in this agreement prior to transfer.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Additional Resources:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://catalog.csus.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>University Catalog</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> for the full listing of degree requirements for this major.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Visit our </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/apply/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Sac State Apply</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> page for more information about our campus!</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Visit the </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/apply/admissions/application-process/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Admissions website</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> for current transfer admission requirements. </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Connect with an </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/apply/admissions/connect-with-admissions.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Admissions Counselor</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">. </span></li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "id": "26766f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "MAJOR INFORMATION",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "22766f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "Students must earn a \"C\" grade or higher in each lower-division course applied to the major. Students who want to declare Criminal Justice as their major at Sacramento State must complete the following prerequisite requirements: Have an overall college GPA of at least a 2.5 or higher, Complete 45 units of transferable coursework, and Complete CRJ 1, CRJ 2, CRJ 4, and CRJ 5 with a grade of \"C\" or higher. The Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Administration of Justice is compatible with the B.S. in Criminal Justice at Sacramento State. Students pursuing the Associate Degree for Transfer must complete all lower-division major coursework with a \"C\" or better. For additional information on applying to the Criminal Justice major, please visit: How to Become a Criminal Justice Major . For additional information, please visit: Department of Criminal Justice .",
      "contentHtml": "<ol><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Students must earn a \"C\" grade or higher in each lower-division course applied to the major.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Students who want to declare Criminal Justice as their major at Sacramento State must complete the following prerequisite requirements:</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Have an overall college GPA of at least a 2.5 or higher,</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Complete 45 units of transferable coursework, and</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Complete CRJ 1, CRJ 2, CRJ 4, and CRJ 5 with a grade of \"C\" or higher. </span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">The Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT) in Administration of Justice is compatible with the B.S. in Criminal Justice at Sacramento State. Students pursuing the Associate Degree for Transfer must complete all lower-division major coursework with a \"C\" or better.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">For additional information on applying to the Criminal Justice major, please visit: </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/college/health-human-services/criminal-justice/applying-to-the-major.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>How to Become a Criminal Justice Major</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">For additional information, please visit: </span><a href=\"https://www.csus.edu/college/health-human-services/criminal-justice/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 14px; color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\"><strong>Department of Criminal Justice</strong></a><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">.</span></li></ol>"
